---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact privacy notice"
  description="Privacy notice for the Hamood Siddiqui portfolio contact form."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Contact form privacy notice.</h1>
      <p class="lead">A concise explanation of what the enquiry form collects and why.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <article class="section narrow prose">
    <h2>Information collected</h2>
    <p>
      The form collects your name, email address, message and consent. Company and project type are
      optional. A hidden anti-spam field and basic request metadata may be processed to prevent abuse.
    </p>
    <h2>Purpose</h2>
    <p>
      The information is used only to understand and respond to your software-development enquiry,
      maintain necessary correspondence and protect the form from spam or misuse.
    </p>
    <h2>Storage and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      The static site submits to a separately configured server. The production handler should send
      mail through an authenticated SMTP provider and retain only the logs necessary for security and
      delivery. Enquiries should not be sold or used for unrelated marketing.
    </p>
    <h2>What not to send</h2>
    <p>
      Do not submit passwords, API keys, health records, financial information or other confidential
      data through the form.
    </p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can contact Hamood through LinkedIn instead of using the form. A public privacy-contact
      email and retention period will be added before production launch.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
